course: dictionary
lesson: 3399
title: Expert
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An expert is a person who knows a lot about a subject or is very skilled at something. When you read, the words around expert are its context, and they give you clues. «Pest experts try to keep animals out first, with sealed gaps and clean kitchens.» Pest experts know how to stop pests, so they are people who know a lot about pests.
explain: Expert can also be an adjective, a describing word. «An expert swimmer» means someone very skilled at swimming. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then swap in your meaning and check it still makes sense.
explain: Experts help us when we cannot do something safely ourselves. «Ask an expert, such as a doctor or an electrician.» Apps let children send photos, and «their photos let experts check what each animal really is». Experts check facts, so their knowledge is worth trusting.
fact: An expert is a person who knows a lot about a subject or is very skilled at something.
fact: «Expert» can also describe someone: «an expert swimmer» is very skilled at swimming.
fact: Useful phrases: expert on, expert at, become an expert, ask an expert.
fact: «Pest experts try to keep animals out first», before using anything dangerous.
fact: Information from real experts is more reliable, but it is still good to check who the expert is and what they know.
exercise: «Their photos let experts check what each animal really is.» What is an expert here? | A very quick runner | *A person who knows a lot about a subject | A person who takes photos | A kind of animal
exercise: «She is an expert swimmer.» What does expert mean in this sentence? | A swimming pool | *Very skilled at swimming | Slow and tired in the water | Afraid of the water
exercise: «Pest experts try to keep animals out first, with sealed gaps and clean kitchens.» What helps keep animals out? | *Sealed gaps and clean kitchens | Loud music | Dangerous things | Pets
test: Information from a real expert is more reliable. What does reliable mean here? | *Can be trusted | Happy and bright | Very loud | Hard to read
test: «Ask an expert, such as a doctor or an electrician, for things you cannot do safely yourself.» When should you ask an expert? | *For something you cannot do safely yourself | For something that is funny | For your favourite colour | For something you already know well
exam: «Mia is an expert on bees.» What does expert on bees mean? | *Someone who knows a lot about bees | A kind of bee that lives in a tree | Someone who keeps bees in a shed | Someone who is afraid of bees
